1795385864313180	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-jjy	{"description":"Exercise the coordination store and operator binding on the named flush-honoring storage profile. Inject loss of unflushed writes at the points specified in plan §9.1, including write, rename and parent-directory flush. Restart from each recovered image.\n\nAcceptance\n- Show the acknowledged commit, revision and audit event recover together. Check binding identity and contents across each boundary. Keep a reproducible fault trace for each failure.\n- Include storage-loss results as well as process-kill results. State the storage assumptions beside the evidence (INV-26).","kind":"task","labels":["m2","test"],"parent":"bn-1hy","size":"m","title":"M2.9.1 Verify durable commits and atomic binding replacement under storage faults"}	blake3:AJWoJ4A-bsU-NQd3xUxiLDq84loRyBra6IsxWTlqKpY
1795385864526457	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ia	{"description":"Use the benchmark manifest from evaluation §12. Record machine, storage profile, budgets, reader count and input sizes for 10,000 leads and 50,000 evidence links.\n\nAcceptance\n- Measure warm entry, show and next at p95 below 300 ms and local mutation through all durable flushes at p95 below 200 ms.\n- Repeat with a slow export and concurrent writes. Record p95 and worst latency, peak memory, WAL high-water and recovery after reader exit. Report the workload and the observed bound.","kind":"task","labels":["m2","test"],"parent":"bn-1hy","size":"m","title":"M2.9.2 Measure CLI latency and WAL growth with a slow snapshot reader"}	blake3:4RmTMELeAZ8XpQVIFbV5smjSeIifD4YoSjF3rt6izyA
