1795385866011300	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-24d	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\n`scourge demo PATH` is the tutorial on the development fixture. `init` may add one owned block to `AGENTS.md`, in Edict's owned-block style, and tracks its digest. The block is short on purpose and is not the enforcement mechanism: the binary works without it.\n\n# Do\n- `demo`: start the fixture, create a workspace, and walk the path of plan §8.2.\n- The managed block text of plan §8.9. Other blocks and user edits are untouched.\n- Generated-example tests: help advertises only what is implemented, and every printed example runs against the demo fixture (INV-34).\n- Never accept a host's trust dialog, disable harness restrictions or install global hooks (INV-43).\n\n# Acceptance (plan §12.2, row M1.8)\n- [ ] Every printed example runs.\n- [ ] No overwrite outside the owned block, tested on an `AGENTS.md` with other blocks and user edits.\n\nDepends on M1.2 and M1.6.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §8.9; INV-34, INV-43.\n\nUpdate the README status and command examples for the delivered M1 surface. Run the documented examples alongside the generated help checks on a fresh demo. Label future commands by milestone so readers can tell which commands are available.\n"}	blake3:fiubWIJSEncnKlXkUt68CbfNCZiUg7heU2PLeczxijs
1795385866132011	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-qx1	{"field":"description","value":"# Acceptance\n- [ ] A generated command reference.\n- [ ] One guide per oracle in the published form: flows, what each rules out, the predicate, the invalid reasons, the known misses.\n- [ ] A plain statement of what shared custody does not prevent.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.later.md §4; notes/plan.md §6.7.\n\nGenerate the reference from the packaged candidate. Run the documented first-use and offline-check examples on a fresh install. A change to the public command catalog or response schema must surface a stale example in the documentation check.\n"}	blake3:8u46wOwa0Ey6FOCBTfG3_na2acssxpU8TTx5tftC44g
1795385866240460	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-26z	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nA consistent backup pauses new runs, snapshots the coordination store with a supported method (never a copy of a live WAL), and takes the evidence store's own export.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Restore goes to an empty destination, starts paused, and never resumes a run or reuses a pass automatically.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §9.4; notes/plan.later.md §4.\n\nCompare source and restored chain heads, record IDs and original evidence digests on the candidate. Check that an in-flight run is visible after restore, still paused with its prior effect status. A nonempty destination is refused without changing its contents. Record the compatible evidence-store version and backup/export capability required by §9.4.\n"}	blake3:YOw4I_biuX1SvqiTgk87GCjJxmAvmZWa1crZBAReKG4
1795385866398279	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1lv	{"field":"description","value":"# Acceptance\n- [ ] A matrix of which instrument versions, which custody topologies on which hosts, and which classes have an oracle.\n- [ ] It is generated from qualification records, not written by hand.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.later.md §4.\n\nGenerate the final rows from qualification evidence for the actual release fingerprint. Each row links its result and distinguishes passed, failed and unmeasured configurations. Test that an absent or skipped qualification cannot produce a supported row.\n"}	blake3:jGXyC_ZP7saw6l5KmoNyTPzVqFuVF-1u0wCNnQNsiCk
1795385866496455	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-2ss	{"field":"description","value":"# Acceptance\n- [ ] Every published claim has its numerator and denominator, per-family results, all attempts, invalid setups, timeouts and model refusals.\n- [ ] First-attempt success and the outcome of all attempts are reported separately.\n- [ ] An unrepresented workflow gets no cold-agent support claim.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.later.md §4; notes/plan.evaluation.md §15.\n\nReconcile the release text with the generated support matrix for the same candidate. Identify unmeasured cells, abstentions, censored trials and per-attempt and all-in costs. Public comparisons require the paired held-out evidence in evaluation §11.\n"}	blake3:zwr51a4oRk_z9KUNqDnDmc63gx0VVlO17IegUHiEHx4
