1795385935108051	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-ijh	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-24d"}	blake3:AYZun4rvU2Ip-rmB0TAJBP4H4RQxXDxhmILAoOF7jW0
1795385935281315	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-2k3	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nThe adversary is the assessed agent, and the agent reads hostile content too. Target responses, repository content, imported reports, filenames and terminal output are untrusted data. Trusted code never interpolates them into commands, instructions or configuration (INV-22).\n\n# Acceptance (plan §12.2, row M2.8)\n- [ ] F-29: forged tool instructions in evidence are stored and shown as inert data.\n- [ ] F-30: poisoned agent configuration in a target repository (`AGENTS.md`, `.mcp.json`, `.claude/`, hooks) is never loaded or followed.\n- [ ] F-31: a simulated model refusal makes the lead `blocked` with reason `model_refused`, and it does not count as tested (INV-24).\n- [ ] Secrets never appear in argv, identifiers, summaries or errors (INV-23).\n\nDepends on M1.2.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §3.3, §8.10; INV-22 to INV-24.\n\n# Size\nFiled at work-package level. M2.0 splits it into child bones after the M1.9 trial.\n\nAdd the hostile-input and secret tests to the M1 functional test entry point. Record environment-dependent skips with their named qualification runner (evaluation §13).\n"}	blake3:mmey5a3yfVelf3rtZmUdcDHyH2qR2v4zp2Loi_73JLU
1795385935469163	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-1td	{"field":"description","value":"Use the producing CLI and shipped evidence store to create the third-party report and bundle. Give a reviewer the export and its instructions on a clean offline machine with the checker. Record producer and recipient versions.\n\nAcceptance\n- Reconcile record IDs, snapshot, custody labels and evidence links across Markdown, JSON and the recipient result. Repeat with an omitted channel and unavailable oracle. Confirm the recipient can locate the bounded claim, caveat, original evidence or declared omission, cleanup and residual effects without coaching.\n- Extend the read-only network-sink suite to the report and bundle checker. Put the checked recipient commands and their result meanings in the user guide. Feed any navigation failures into the report changes before close. The separate maintainer-decision pilot stays in M2.10.\n\nSee plan §10 and evaluation §13–14."}	blake3:uAyhwcPZ9NJwjz2zPqx4nZCqk7VWbuKThbucnTEoCiM
1795385935837646	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-96y	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nnotes/ holds about 600 KB of history: plan.rev1.md (superseded), plan.review.1.md to plan.review.6.md, and plan.disposition.md. They are kept because the disposition cites the reviews line by line and the reviews cite revision 1. Every agent that opens notes/ pays to read them. Git keeps them at commit 172af34 and earlier.\n\n# Do\nAfter the owner has answered the pending calls, remove those eight files from the working tree, update the README's Documents section and plan.md's header and §16 to point at the commit, and keep one short paragraph on how to print them (`git show COMMIT:notes/FILE`).\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] notes/ holds plan.md, plan.evaluation.md, plan.later.md and plan.research.md only.\n- [ ] README and plan.md name the commit where the history lives. No dangling links.\n\n# Status\nProposed by the audit. Owner decision.\n\nThe owner's decision on archiving the files is distinct from answers about the design. If archiving is accepted, pin a commit containing the actual versions being removed, including the final disposition, and verify that the retrieval instruction works for each path. If declined, record that decision and retain the documents.\n"}	blake3:49hvSgNY4XYmYEkHN3wogtmD9Gnt68JKM7Pl4S5ZUto
1795385936155597	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-2d7	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nA ceremony audit on 2026-11-22 found the plan ready to build from and still being revised: seven commits, all documentation, and no code. Revision 5 followed no review. The plan also calls §13 \"the requirements\" while D13, M0.4 and §17 say obligations and fixtures are justified against the baseline taxonomy before anything freezes.\n\n# Do (about ten lines of edits in notes/plan.md, no new revision of the design)\n- Header: revision 5 is frozen. The next revision happens only on M0 evidence (the M0.1 inventory or the M0.4 taxonomy). Questions that come up before then go in a short open-questions list.\n- §13 and §14: one sentence saying the invariants and fixtures are candidates that the M0.4 ADR keeps, cuts or adds.\n- §17 and §12.1: name the premise rehearsal (M0.0) as the first step.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] The three edits are in notes/plan.md and nothing else in the design changed.\n\n# Status\nProposed by the audit. Not yet approved by the owner: confirm before doing it.\n\nRecord the owner's decision on the proposed freeze note. If declined, close this proposal with the decision and leave the design as approved. The M0 evidence review can proceed under revision 5.\n"}	blake3:FUndpuHJ5q73SXoo4THPu7GpzJJzGx9Ao7LasXhBByI
1795385936514726	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-73w	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nThe M1 bones were written from plan revision 5, before any measurement. Use revision 5 and any owner-approved freeze note as the baseline.\n\n# Do\n- Update notes/plan.md once, as revision 6, from the M0.1 inventory, the M0.4.5 ADR and the frozen contracts. This is the only revision M0 produces.\n- Go through every M1 bone: close what the M0 decision cut, fix what the contracts changed, split anything that is now clearly too large.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Every open M1 bone matches the frozen contracts.\n- [ ] Bones cut by the M0 decision are closed with a comment that names the ADR.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §12.1, §12.3.\n"}	blake3:QghN3_yjCPd1Hv_l0ryvXYAip5bR0hqSC5eDg-ic1VY
1795385936789003	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-73w	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nThe M1 bones were written from plan revision 5, before any measurement. Use revision 5 and any owner-approved freeze note as the baseline.\n\n# Do\n- Reconcile notes/plan.md with the M0.1 inventory, the M0.4.5 ADR and the frozen contracts. Apply the owner's decision on the freeze note and record any resulting revision.\n- Go through every M1 bone: close what the M0 decision cut, fix what the contracts changed, split anything that is now clearly too large.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Every open M1 bone matches the frozen contracts.\n- [ ] Bones cut by the M0 decision are closed with a comment that names the ADR.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §12.1, §12.3.\n"}	blake3:4cesMlsBvdoFOCsB1NAYpGuRgnIAHWFqNvdWTngdW1c
1795385937719455	codex-groom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1we	{"description":"Write the short entry note called for in plan.later.md. Use the M4 outcome to name the proposed release scope, required packaging and migration evidence, custody/host configurations and owner of the held-out corpus. Re-cut the large M5.1 and M5.2 packages after the cost and scope are known.\n\nAcceptance\n- Map the claimed support cells to qualification records and identify missing inputs.\n- Name the packaged candidate, docs and evaluation inputs that must be fingerprinted together before scoring. Record the criteria for requalification if the candidate changes.\n- Carry the resulting scope and dependencies into the existing M5 bones. Keep held-out material under its independent owner.\n\nSee plan.later.md introduction and §4, and evaluation §5–7 and §11.","kind":"task","labels":["m5","plan"],"parent":"bn-109","size":"s","title":"M5.0 Fix the release scope and qualification inputs from M4 results","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:x6BJE6DzWnN7PmH0TD-mvM3vhnRvEzolZO5aXB1XT94
