1795386775477359	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-9eo	{"description":"# Context\nM0.6.2 and M1.4 wait on Investigation's recording API (W07), and the owner decided Scourge uses it as shipped (plan §15.2). When bn-ws2 was written, W07 was open in Investigation's milestone B and its crate was a stub. Asking for the schedule at the end of M0 (where M0.7.4 first put it) is too late to change anything.\n\n# Do\nIn Investigation's tracker, ask for W07 (over W01 to W03 and the minimum of W06) to be scheduled first within milestone B. Name the Scourge packages that wait on it and the operations they need: begin, append, attach, finalize, recover.\n\n# Limits\nDo not ask for anything ahead of Investigation's Milestone A gate (plan §15.2 item 1). This is a scheduling request inside milestone B.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] The request is filed and linked here, and bn-ws2 has a comment pointing to it.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §9.2, §12.1 (\"Prerequisite\"), §15.2.","kind":"task","labels":["evidence","m0","upstream"],"parent":"bn-2lu","size":"xs","title":"M0.6.0 Ask Investigation to schedule W07 first inside its milestone B"}	blake3:EMmcdA1TskOeM4xk0TlT97n3cCVGYZGy3INpL9zT2Bo
1795386775506186	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-5l8	{"description":"# Context\nThe plan's revisit trigger (§15.2 item 4): if Investigation's W07 has not shipped when Scourge's M0.1 to M0.5 are done, the owner looks at the dependency again, with Investigation's tracker counts and Scourge's M0 results in hand. Before this bone, the trigger was only a note inside bn-ws2, and nothing in the tracker would come up when it fired. M0 cannot close without M0.6.2, and M0.6.2 waits on W07.\n\n# Do\nWhen M0.1 to M0.5 are closed:\n- If W07 has shipped: close this bone with the Investigation version and a link to M0.6.2.\n- If not: collect Investigation's tracker counts (open, done, W07 state) and the M0 results (taxonomy, custody outcome), and ask the owner to decide. The trigger reopens nothing by itself.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] The owner's decision, or the shipped W07 version, is recorded here.\n- [ ] Any change to the dependency is carried into M0.6.2, M1.4 and the M0.7.5 re-cut.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §15.2 (items 1 and 4); bn-ws2.","kind":"task","labels":["evidence","m0","owner","plan"],"parent":"bn-2lu","size":"s","title":"M0.6.3 Owner: revisit the Investigation dependency if W07 has not shipped when M0.1 to M0.5 are done"}	blake3:pm8WWr5bfTMOdnHswHgz8lj8nt4IkYFNzdrc_48zP_0
1795386790931981	gauntlet-dev	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-2r5	{"field":"description","value":"# Context\nA blocker is work: if the instrument lacks an operation, add the smallest general capability upstream or restrict the feature (plan §12.4). Each request rests on a fact found in M0.1, so it is filed as soon as that fact is known, not at the end of M0. Upstream lead time is on M1's critical path: M1.3.2 and M1.7 need the per-send reference.\n\n# Do\nFile, each with a reproduction and the Scourge feature it gates:\n- Teapot: a per-send reference the verifier can look up after a lost response (gap found in M0.1.3).\n- Teapot or Hallpass: run-level attribution of ledger units, a caller reference at spend time (M0.1.2 block draws, M0.1.6 two projects on one pass).\n- Teapot: a send mode that bypasses rules, intercepts and hooks and records that it did, only if M0.1.5 found one that reaches a verifier send.\n\nFiled elsewhere:\n- The loopback-enforcement blocker is filed by M0.5.4 with its reproduction.\n- The Investigation W07 scheduling request is M0.6.0.\n\n# Acceptance\n- [ ] Each request is filed in the owning repository's tracker and linked here.\n- [ ] A request that M0.1 showed is not needed is listed here with the evidence, not filed.\n\nRefs: notes/plan.md §7.2, §7.4, §12.2 (row M0.7), §12.4."}	blake3:C-QYluyJNvFlcdLC9Az1SpIZBFa7VY0PqNvbUl52xyI
