1795407290192804	outcome-contract	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2wv	{"body":"All four acceptance P1s fixed in 0297a7bcf418559d1b8bc1ed692ff1d4933953a6 after clean Maw sync to main 794cd2efb17c3d45ecb8bb8e44115e295cd3681d. Eligibility now enforces the complete frozen configured state, nested arrays/objects fail closed, PassReport upstream_proxy is selected and schema-tested, and qualification/evidence commits reproducible setup commands, pinned schemas, raw inventories/hashes, projected outputs, creation evidence and cleanup for two real fresh projects. The raw inventories differ; both are eligible and project to fb51e939916d35e52ae26d383200f254c054ff53d56c1f4318add9da5689a3c6. just baseline-check and full just check pass post-sync; no baseline agent or target request ran and no pycache exists. Seal cr-2etlqi retargeted/re-requested; Rite anchor 01M839SYKS34YQTD95HN70ZRTH. Claims and workspace retained."}	blake3:OmKa6M4GmKKYQZbgXXq1EZSnDnVd_psihazf33rkq84
1795408064107236	orca-cyber	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"Implemented and committed the local acceptance matrix in workspace bn-2cu.\n\nCommit: 350ee127f6109907c80e1752c0de3be898e90e0e\nReview: cr-22j00n (open, reviewer scourge-security; base 8d43996..target 350ee12, exactly one commit)\n\nResult: all eight fixed payloads are refused in isolated custody with separate principals. Isolated custody with shared principals permits only attempt 06 (owner sharing state), so the target can share the verifier's object (F-40); attempts 01-05, 07 and 08 stay refused. Shared custody permits all eight. Attempts 07/08 report the instrument edit surface and verifier-session reach; they do not prove a rule alters a direct send.\n\nAttempt 06 ran with separate resets and an owner-create/other-read control before and during an active verifier run, unheld and held. The hold is not required: the unheld during-run attempt is already refused in isolated+separate. The hold refused the scripted attempt in every configuration, but it is not a boundary in shared custody where host network access bypasses the relay.\n\nEvidence: fixtures/contracts/tamper-matrix-observed.json (sanitized; verdicts, statuses, counters and stable hashes only) and docs/tamper-matrix.md (attempt-by-configuration table, host/tool pins, limits). Configurations are proved materially distinct by worker probes, account isolation and attempt outcomes. Pinned Teapot 6d15d6, Hallpass be2895, cached image 28eb0c, rootless Podman 6.1.3, kernel 7.2.8-arch1-2; no network downloads. CID-only container removal verified for 6/6 containers per isolated configuration; both engines and the fixture were verified stopped. The retained /tmp/scourge-topology-m9zqviiq directory and other workspaces were not touched.\n\nTests: scripts/test-tamper-matrix.py 27 passed; scripts/test-candidate-topology.py 3 passed; just tamper-check 8 passed; just check passed.\n\nLimits: one local host, eight fixed payloads, no enforcement, no model agent. Not proof against arbitrary adversaries.\n\nNot done/merged/pushed; workspace not destroyed; claims on bone://scourge/bn-2cu and workspace://scourge/bn-2cu are retained for the tech lead's independent review."}	blake3:h7uNB4lOkMfhxSG2R--ZtZvx5Qrf6tg_OxxFohBdNcQ
1795408383058993	orca-cyber	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"Corrected the hold interpretation after independent review and retargeted the review.\n\nWorkspace synced onto current main 794cd2ef (rebased the matrix commit cleanly; AGENTS.md classifier-handoff change preserved, review log preserved).\nFinal commit: 0db4e824247d728b5ffb7635f1e73d9453e82469 (1299290 rebased matrix + 0db4e82 hold fix).\nReview: cr-22j00n retargeted to base 794cd2efb17c3d45ecb8bb8e44115e295cd3681d -> target 0db4e82, reviewer scourge-security. A review thread on docs/tamper-matrix.md:93 records the correction.\n\nHold result is now hold.required: true. Isolated custody with shared principals succeeds unheld during the active run and is refused when the hold is applied, so the hold is retained for that vulnerable configuration. The qualified isolated+separate topology does not itself need the hold (qualified_configuration_requires_hold: false). The hold does not repair before-run contamination: the before-run unheld trial also succeeds in isolated_shared. It is not a security boundary in shared custody, where host network access bypasses the relay; that window is recorded but not claimed as containment.\n\nAttempt matrix unchanged: all eight refused in isolated+separate; isolated+shared permits only attempt 06 (F-40); shared custody permits all eight. Evidence fixtures/contracts/tamper-matrix-observed.json and docs/tamper-matrix.md were regenerated live with pinned Teapot 6d15d6, Hallpass be2895, cached image 28eb0c, rootless Podman 6.1.3, kernel 7.2.8-arch1-2. CID-only cleanup verified 6/6 containers per isolated configuration; engines and fixture verified stopped; /tmp/scourge-topology-m9zqviiq and other workspaces untouched.\n\nTests on the final commit: scripts/test-tamper-matrix.py 29 passed (includes an exact regression that isolated_shared alone makes the hold required while the qualified topology does not need it); scripts/test-candidate-topology.py 3 passed; just tamper-check 8 passed; just check passed.\n\nLimitations: eight fixed local payloads, one loopback host, no enforcement, no model agent; the retained hold covers only the scripted relay path; not proof against arbitrary adversaries.\n\nNot marked done, not merged, not destroyed, not pushed; claims on bone://scourge/bn-2cu and workspace://scourge/bn-2cu are retained for the tech lead's independent review."}	blake3:arD7y-zMW4HG7El0kBaj80GTc9gSN_EhpE6hJj8k6lk
1795408603063028	outcome-contract	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2wv	{"body":"Re-review fixes committed at e2bcc9597d049e006745cdc23f9b132086c0a59b after Maw sync confirmed main epoch 794cd2efb17c3d45ecb8bb8e44115e295cd3681d. Eligibility now rejects wrong project config links, non-loopback listeners, log/script error-drop counters, watch edits, and current-digest drift; structured nested fields fail closed; wildcard matching requires an ASCII index in an actual list. Qualification captures and validates schemas for all 24 commands, cross-checks raw project IDs/paths/digests, and requires proxy/root cleanup success. Fresh twins remain eligible with distinct raw hashes/IDs and equal semantic digest 05aab34cb8c97a930ee7abd86224299ad0e1198e5c9f33910b1aeb5b25a083cd; all cleanup succeeded; assessment agents and target requests remain zero. Post-sync just baseline-check and full just check pass (13 focused tests). Seal cr-2etlqi retargeted/re-requested at exact commit; claims/workspace retained and no pycache remains."}	blake3:vc1G6Vobbczw4KR0R3O05q5N0ZAgV4LXh-EDfJNs-ko
