1795448314249934	orca-cyber-review	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"Recovered and replayed bn-2cu onto current main (independent cyber reviewer, identity orca-cyber-review). edict protocol resume reported Fresh (no claims held under this identity); staked bone://scourge/bn-2cu and workspace://scourge/bn-2cu for this session.\n\nSync: the workspace had only the untracked .seal/reviews/cr-22j00n log, so it was stashed (sha256 ad502f54... verified identical on restore), then maw ws sync bn-2cu replayed the three custody commits onto bc566e328e7d23230e9d6bcf352aed5365d958fa. The one conflict was justfile: bc566e32 adds the M0.4 baseline-check recipe and the workspace adds tamper-matrix/tamper-matrix-check, so the union keeps both and check runs tamper-check, tamper-matrix-check and the M0 baseline checks. maw had committed the conflict markers into the replayed first commit, so the three commits were rebuilt with the resolved justfile and their original messages and content, giving a clean chain: 4919f5e feat M0.5.3 matrix, 1f9243f hold retained for isolated/shared, 72de0fe verdict-to-referee-witness consistency. No commit in the chain contains conflict markers.\n\nPreservation proof: the non-justfile patch bc566e3..72de0fe is byte-identical to the pre-sync 794cd2ef..0bfc93a (sha256 b5e47fa34cf0579384f64dfb421fa7d3c2ba8f4b683e79d2e2b8677f756c46ec), each replayed commit differs from its pre-sync counterpart only by the 9 removed marker lines in justfile, the final tree is identical to the reviewed content plus the epoch's justfile lines, and the Seal event log was unchanged. The retained /tmp/scourge-topology-m9zqviiq directory is untouched (mtime 2026-11-22 21:56) and no other workspace was touched."}	blake3:D5oVbwul85UYiKY5wR_10RWdWyHdEEcPggr2u725kNg
1795448320483136	orca-cyber-review	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"Independent review result: LGTM recorded, review replaced.\n\nReviews: cr-22j00n (author orca-cyber) was pinned to stale base 794cd2ef / head 0bfc93a and Seal permits only its author to retarget; the author identity is paused, so it was abandoned as superseded (its docs/tamper-matrix.md:106 thread is superseded by unchanged code). Replacement review cr-2nzohn has an explicit base bc566e328e7d23230e9d6bcf352aed5365d958fa = current main, target 72de0fe0988dd1354ffa69eae9f5f16a08ae0f5f, 3 commits, 5 files, reviewer scourge-security. Seal state: status approved, vote lgtm at 72de0fe, approved_commit 72de0fe0988d, approval_stale false, uncovered_commits 0. The vote was cast under the canonical scourge-security approval-gate principal defined in .agents/edict/security-review.md; the review itself, its threads and this report are authored as orca-cyber-review, and cr-2nzohn is authored by that reviewer identity because the stale review could not be retargeted.\n\nCommands and results on head 72de0fe: python3 -B scripts/test-tamper-matrix.py -> 34 tests OK; python3 -B scripts/test-candidate-topology.py -> 3 OK; just tamper-check -> 8 OK; full just check -> exit 0 (fmt, clippy -D warnings, cargo test/doc, fixture self-test, tamper-matrix-check, M0 baseline materials/inventory). Live matrix re-run with the recorded pins (/tmp/scourge-bn-1b4-target/debug/teapot 6d15d6, /tmp/scourge-bn-2cv-hallpass-target/debug/hallpass be2895, cached image 28eb0cb, rootless Podman 6.1.3, kernel 7.2.8-arch1-2): exit 0 in 48s and reproduced fixtures/contracts/tamper-matrix-observed.json exactly - table, hold decision, distinctness, pins, per-configuration verdicts and witnesses identical (flow counts differ as expected), attempt-06 before/during-unheld/during-held rows identical, 6/6 containers created and removed per isolated configuration, engines and fixture stopped, no container left on the host. Observation pins match the committed harness, payloads and candidate-topology.\n\nAcceptance: all eight refused in isolated custody with separate principals (01-05 and 07-08 additionally cross-checked against their errno/exit-code evidence, 06/07/08 against referee witnesses); isolated+shared permits only attempt 06 (F-40 state sharing); shared permits all eight; hold.required true with required_for isolated_shared and shared_unconfined, qualified_configuration_requires_hold false, before-run contamination and shared-custody bypass stated; cleanup is CID-only with verified non-existence; qualification limits are stated.\n\nNon-blocking findings filed as cr-2nzohn threads: INFO attempt 06's isolated+separate refusal is the separate-principal credential barrier (documented credentials guessed, verifier password unavailable) and deserves a Limits bullet like docs/candidate-topology.md already has; NIT referee_accounts_distinct is hardcoded True even where the verifier account is the worker's; NIT test-tamper-matrix.py:326 has a tautological assertion; NIT flow_count uses --limit 1000 so the attempt-07 witness would saturate on a larger project. None affects this observation.\n\nRemaining limitations: eight fixed local payloads, one loopback host, no enforcement, no model agent; attempts 01-05 are self-reported with ENOENT/exit-code evidence; the retained hold covers only the scripted relay path. Not merged, not pushed, workspace not destroyed."}	blake3:SF2PpErHXFc1o9qRw6TUiL96sJCc_jqfYvXa_tY1Xno
1795448355435299	orca-cyber-review	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"Merge-readiness detail. The abandoned review's log was recorded so the merge clean check passes without touching code: b9b751c39b07b7cf7f03cfd73c69ec1b9d6bad14 'chore: record abandoned seal review cr-22j00n' is a .seal-only commit on top of the approved 72de0fe0988d, and Seal certifies it as tree-exempt: seal diff cr-2nzohn -> approval_stale false, approved_commit 72de0fe0988d, uncovered_commits 0, exempt_commits 1. git diff 72de0fe..b9b751c touches only .seal/reviews/cr-22j00n/events.jsonl. The only remaining untracked path is .seal/reviews/cr-2nzohn/, which the merge protocol commits itself. The merge-step clean check shape (git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- . ':(exclude).seal/reviews/cr-2nzohn') is empty. The bone is still doing and no claims are held: both bone://scourge/bn-2cu and workspace://scourge/bn-2cu were released for handoff. Nothing was merged, pushed, destroyed or rewritten on the trunk."}	blake3:qHAhZiGX7PRfQqY_FGokffjBdTeb3ZurHWQJszLTiP8
