1795448967143160	scourge-dev	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"Canonical Daybreak review cr-29245f BLOCKED exact head b9b751c39b07. HIGH th-1pddef: scripts/tamper-matrix.py qualified() accepts unsupported as equivalent to refused, so accepted=true/exit 0 can occur without exercising all eight required attempts; test-tamper-matrix.py currently preserves the false pass. Required fix: isolated_separate qualification must require every verdict exactly refused; held unsupported trials must remain unsupported rather than be relabeled refused; regressions must prove unsupported makes accepted false and command nonzero. Dedicated reviewer completed through Agentbus and was terminated; review claim released."}	blake3:NjZ7xj4t7W0Xukymdefr4mZBMTi_cPiPOhUdiEGyn_I
1795449156613669	orca-cyber-fix	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"orca-cyber-fix: acceptance-integrity fix committed for canonical HIGH th-1pddef (cr-29245f). Exact HEAD 29d5040e3b5184817706d38f759962178c663283 on top of the blocked head b9b751c39b07 (4 files, +121/-27); no retarget, no vote, no merge, no push, no Rite verdict, workspace not destroyed.\n\nFix: scripts/tamper-matrix.py qualified() now requires every isolated_separate verdict to be exactly refused (was refused-or-unsupported), and the top-level isolated_separate_all_attempts_failed field carries the same exact-refusal predicate (was verdict != succeeded). Held unsupported trials at the flagged handling path stay unsupported: held_trials_refused and during_run_attempt_blocked_by_hold now require exactly refused, and the new held_trial_verdicts map records the true verdict. Acceptance assembly moved into qualification() and the exit status into exit_status(), so main() returns 1 whenever accepted is false. This closes the false pass where a missing/malformed precondition yielded accepted=true and exit 0 with fewer than eight exercised attempts.\n\nRegressions (scripts/test-tamper-matrix.py, 34 -> 39 tests): test_unsupported_is_not_a_refusal (replaces the false-pass test that asserted qualified==True); test_unsupported_makes_accepted_false_and_the_command_nonzero (unsupported 03 -> qualified false, all_attempts_failed false, accepted false, exit_status 1); test_every_attempt_refused_still_accepts_and_exits_zero; test_held_unsupported_trial_stays_unsupported (held unsupported is neither refused nor blocked by the hold); committed hold/acceptance blocks must reproduce from the retained configurations. Non-vacuity checked: against the pre-fix predicates these three regressions fail (qualified True, accepted True), so they do pin the defect.\n\nEvidence preserved: the eight fixed payloads are untouched (pins.payload_sha256 unchanged) and the retained live observation is unchanged apart from pins.harness_sha256 (fc2205bd... -> 95a3ada6...) and the new hold.held_trial_verdicts (all three configurations refused, matching the retained during-held trials). All eight isolated/separate verdicts stay refused; accepted stays true on the retained evidence. docs/tamper-matrix.md:199-202 now states unsupported is never a refusal and makes accepted false/nonzero.\n\nTests on 29d5040: python3 -B scripts/test-tamper-matrix.py 39 OK; scripts/test-candidate-topology.py 3 OK; just tamper-check 8 OK; full just check exit 0. git diff --check clean; merge-step clean-check shape (excluding the untracked .seal/reviews/cr-2nzohn and cr-29245f logs) is empty. The retained /tmp/scourge-topology-m9zqviiq directory and other workspaces were not touched. No live matrix run was needed and none was performed; no payload, token or secret was changed.\n\nClaims bone://scourge/bn-2cu and workspace://scourge/bn-2cu remain held under orca-cyber-fix. Next tech-lead action: independently re-review b9b751c..29d5040 (or the full bc566e3..29d5040 range), then decide whether to retarget cr-29245f to 29d5040 and re-review, or open a fresh review; then resolve th-1pddef's block and merge only through edict protocol merge. Do not treat this comment as a review verdict."}	blake3:la3aaQQVKKpGzusoXYmZ9WG7NLwu8OZR4tl_mcXn66A
1795449989731548	orca-cyber-recapture	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2cu	{"body":"orca-cyber-recapture: live recapture committed for cr-29245f/th-3pl3z8 (MEDIUM). Exact HEAD 7b97c5a4 on top of 29d5040e; one file changed, +15/-15, the observation only. No retarget, no vote, no merge, no push, no Rite verdict, workspace not destroyed, retained evidence and other workspaces untouched. Claims bone://scourge/bn-2cu and workspace://scourge/bn-2cu staked for this identity (the earlier orca-cyber-fix claims had expired).\n\nCommand (exact, from this workspace, exit 0 in 57s, stdout committed unchanged):\n  python3 -B scripts/tamper-matrix.py \\\n    --teapot /tmp/scourge-bn-1b4-target/debug/teapot \\\n    --hallpass /tmp/scourge-bn-2cv-hallpass-target/debug/hallpass \\\n    > /tmp/bn-2cu-recapture/observation.json\nPins used and re-verified in the observation: Teapot 6d15d625e10afa768a221f64eb7a2a245a64a7babbe61cf74ce8d4ff33b2f458, Hallpass be289583707b9a6810d148dbddf4e3c0c09fddd74b78d4e00cab47f8c30e993d, image 28eb0cb65acb65b970e85c0dc57d10067868fae8dd00d072413df273132123ac, rootless Podman 6.1.3, kernel 7.2.8-arch1-2, rustc 1.100.0 (0ef1bc386 2026-11-09). The harness refuses any other binary digest, a non-rootless Podman or a missing cached image, so an unpinned reuse fails closed.\n\nProvenance now comes from one invocation. recorded_at_utc is 2026-11-23T16:05:34Z (run window 16:04:35Z-16:05:32Z), and pins.harness_sha256 is 95a3ada670880445511555caa3d8446edd841159b188b4c80dca54f750a25146, which is sha256 of the exact committed scripts/tamper-matrix.py bytes at 7b97c5a; pins.payload_sha256, pins.candidate_topology_sha256 (c48a7957...), pins.teapot/hallpass and pins.fixture_sha256 (d1a4cae9...) are unchanged. Committed observation sha256 168635c1e2e99358f5c08592a0caf0f051be66ccfd74d7250c42e882c5132f1e and byte-identical (cmp) to the harness stdout; nothing in it was edited afterwards.\n\nOutcome comparison against the previously committed observation: identical for every semantic field - pins, host, limits, matrix, schema_version, table (rows and markdown), distinct (proved, axes, pairwise differences), qualified (accepted true, all eight isolated/separate verdicts 01-08 refused, configuration_isolated_separate_qualified true) and hold (required true, required_for isolated_shared and shared_unconfined, required_for_isolated_custody isolated_shared, held_trial_verdicts all refused, before-run contamination flags, shared-custody bypass). A full recursive diff finds 15 changed leaves only: recorded_at_utc, attempt-06 interleaved send counters (isolated_separate during 9/10 -> 11/12 and 28/29 -> 14/15, isolated_shared 15/16 -> 12/13 and 15/16 -> 13/13, all with errors 0, interleaved true, attempts still refused), verifier flow counts (75 -> 63 and 68 -> 62, delta 0 both) and the identity flow-list digests. The attempt-06 before/during-unheld/during-held rows, verdicts, referee witnesses and stand-in flags are unchanged.\n\nCleanup proof from this run: containers_created 6 / containers_removed 6 for isolated_separate and for isolated_shared, 0/0 for shared_unconfined (no container), engines_stopped true and fixture_stopped true in all three configurations, validated before emission; removal is CID-only from --cidfile with podman container exists returning not-found. Post-run podman ps -a on this host lists no containers, and no scourge-topology-* run directory was retained (the successful run cleaned its own).\n\nPreservation: the eight fixed payloads are byte-unchanged (pins.payload_sha256 map identical, git diff touches no scripts/), and /tmp/scourge-topology-m9zqviiq is untouched (mtime 2026-11-22 21:56:48, tree digest fe674a344ff3fc95cdba3c6e14f87234abbd9ffa8b06bc1c6a3af07676f15af6 before and after). No other workspace was touched. docs/tamper-matrix.md needed no change: its host/tool pins, cleanup wording and unsupported-is-not-a-refusal rule already describe the recaptured observation.\n\nTests on 7b97c5a: python3 -B scripts/test-tamper-matrix.py 39 passed; python3 -B scripts/test-candidate-topology.py 3 passed; python3 -B scripts/test-tamper-attempts.py (just tamper-check) 8 passed; full just check exit 0 (fmt, clippy -D warnings, cargo test/doc, fixture self-test, candidate topology, tamper-check, tamper-matrix-check, M0 baseline materials/inventory, deps-check). git diff --check clean; merge-step clean-check shape excluding the untracked .seal/reviews/cr-29245f and cr-2nzohn logs is empty.\n\nNext tech-lead action: independently re-review bc566e3..7b97c5a (or 29d5040..7b97c5a for the recapture alone), confirm th-3pl3z8 is answered by live provenance rather than a renamed pin, then retarget or replace cr-29245f if required and merge only through edict protocol merge. Do not treat this comment as a review verdict."}	blake3:cbvw4c0cV7HjNWBt1W4KfsrouzeUUsAr7DS3xkJkaes
