1795468340320804	scourge-dev	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2yt	{"body":"Completed the full M0.7.1 contract freeze in workspace bn-2yt at HEAD b29acd6699de92408d098f2a35e09de6720234fa (parent dc53f9a). Working tree clean; bone stays doing. No review, merge, push, claim release or workspace teardown.\n\nFiles (11 added): schemas/engagement.v1.schema.json (scourge.engagement.v1), schemas/policy-rule.v1.schema.json (scourge.policy-rule.v1), schemas/claim-template.v1.schema.json (scourge.claim-template.v1), fixtures/target/schema-examples/engagement.toml, fixtures/target/schema-examples/policy-rule-orders.json, fixtures/target/schema-examples/claim-template-private-object-read.json, scripts/check-schema-contracts.py, docs/adr/engagement-schema.md, docs/adr/policy-rule-schema.md, docs/adr/claim-template-schema.md, justfile (schema-check recipe, wired into check).\n\nScope: the engagement contract now covers engagement metadata, both principals with identity probe and optional verifier_session, and all 12 development fixture properties with read, write, plant, remove, readers, writers and policy (write/writers only where the fixture has the write route). Every operational field is an inert registered reference (pass, project, version, session, group, operation, resource, selector). No request line, method, route, host, port, credential, payload, script or dispatch grammar is encoded. Policy rules type engagement/document/operator/inferred sources, require operator admission for the three admitted forms, and bind property plus target version. The claim template models typed slots with suppliers, an ordered recipe of registered-operation IDs with slot bindings, per-step effect class and controls, an oracle bound to its claim scope, cleanup evidence and both retest dimensions. M0.4.5 dispositions applied: object-read class keeps object_read scope (collection/existence need own classes and stay leads), property slots operator-only (INV-36), shared custody admits only attributed statements, cleanup is the plant effect class (INV-40). The prior offline review subset (engagement-review/policy-rule/claim-template-review schemas, engagement-review.toml, check-review-schemas.py, engagement-review-schemas.md) was uncommitted at dc53f9a and is replaced; every constraint it encoded is retained by the new contracts and the new check.\n\nChecks: just schema-check 11 tests OK (positive examples plus negative cases for missing fields, invalid references, source/provenance errors, scope/oracle mismatches, forbidden executable-shaped content, strict JSON/TOML parsing, schema keyword/strictness audit; policy example digest recomputed from the engagement example); just fixture-check OK (12 resource classes, identity probes, referee catalog, external package); just check exit 0 end to end (baseline, realapp, tamper, tamper-matrix, deps, fmt, offline clippy, cargo tests, evidence self-tests); just dry-run confirms schema-check runs inside check. The operational verifier input contract (capability binding, dispatch) remains open by design and is not encoded here."}	blake3:ALVcB4ulzuToAgLp0i9x5dj21shHg5lsvm99TBA-mNY
1795468595547192	m07-oracle-codex	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-ggt	{"body":"Ready for lead handoff at a6946d1d4a9c7722760fdd4e366836248b4828e0 in clean workspace bn-ggt. Frozen docs/adr/oracle-specifications.md and docs/contracts/oracle-specifications.v1.json for web.private-object-read.v1 and web.forbidden-state-change.v1, plus just oracle-spec-check and 12 negative/positive checker tests. The registry lists 23 numbered mutation checks, exact flows/predicates/invalid reasons/known misses, and M0-ADD-03 collection/existence scope refusal before traffic. Passed just oracle-spec-check and final full just check. The first sandboxed full run stopped in existing candidate-topology process tests; the same tests and both full final runs passed outside the sandbox. Contract explicitly remains contract_only; live M1/M2 oracle and mutation implementation is downstream. No review, merge, closure, push, claim release or workspace destruction performed."}	blake3:-38_xS_6JH-Q_TAytJIMDCbLqJoITYZ1U7NlDG8m_9I
